 "interpretation": "The song reflects the sádhaka's resolve to overcome the pull of máyá (the material world). The attractive sensory objects are characterized as worthless playthings (asár khelná). People in the world wander in ignorance: some are concealed by the darkness of ignorance (meghe gherá), others are blinded by the appeal of the transient light of máyá (cáṋder áloy hárá), while others are entangled in the coils of egotism and delusion. The majority fear the hardships of the path and forget the true spiritual goal of their existence.",
